[%- sections.title = "Set Up Two-Factor Authentication" -%]
[%- CALL dw.active_resource_group( "foundation" ) -%]

<form method="POST">
    [%- dw.form_auth -%]
    [%- form.hidden( name = "mode", value = "submit" ) -%]

<fieldset>
<legend>Getting Ready for 2FA</legend>

<p>
    To set up two-factor authentication (2FA), you will need the following:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>An authenticator application that supports time-based one-time passwords (TOTP).</li>
    <li>A secure notepad or way to save your <strong>recovery codes</strong>. These are important,
        if you lose your 2FA device these codes are how you will get back in to your account!</li>
</ol>

</fieldset>
<fieldset>
<legend>Check Your Apps Before Enabling</legend>
<p>After you enable 2FA, apps and services will no longer be able to sign in to this account with
its password alone. This includes authenticated feeds, posting clients, backups, and services
that import from or crosspost to this account.</p>
<p>For clients that support API keys, create a key on your <a href="[% site.root %]/api">API page</a>
and configure the client to use it before enabling 2FA. An API key grants access without an
authentication code, so keep it private. A client that cannot use an API key may stop working
with this account. Accounts where you leave 2FA disabled are unchanged.</p>
</fieldset>
<fieldset>
<legend>Setting Up Your Device</legend>

<div class='row'>
<div class='large-8 columns'>
    Now scan this QR code in your authentication application:
</div>
<div class='large-4 columns'>
    [%- form.hidden( name='totp_secret', value=totp_secret ) -%]
    <p>Setup key: <code>[% totp_secret | html %]</code></p>
    <img src='[% qrcode | html %]' alt='QR code for setting up 2FA'/>
</div>
</div>

</fieldset>
<fieldset>
<legend>Verify & Enable</legend>

<div class='row'>
<div class='large-8 columns'>
    Finally, please enter a generated 2FA code from your device:
</div>
<div class='large-4 columns'>
    [% form.textbox(name='verification_code', maxlength='6') %]
</div></div>

<p>Confirm your account password: [% form.password(name='password') %]</p>
<p>Enabling two-factor authentication signs this account out in other browsers. This browser stays signed in. Save your recovery codes.</p>
[% form.submit(name='action:enable', value='Enable Two-Factor Authentication') %]

</fieldset>
</form>
